 trigger so the ack returned before disconnect): captured pre-restart boot_id and service health, waited for SSH to drop then return, confirmed each boot_id changed (node1 738d0aac→60f8e0a5, node2 2fc81aed→f993fede, node3 0d6209e2→9029646e), and re-verified firewalld state/zone config and the node2-allow/node3-reject/SSH-allow behavior after all reboots completed.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/firewalld (RHEL 7.9, firewalld 0.6.3, active+enabled, ssh already allowed in public zone)","Attempted rich-rule priority approach; failed because firewalld 0.6.3 lacks the priority attribute (added in 0.7.0)","Created permanent source-based zone node2only with source 10.100.140.11/32 and port 9000/tcp allowed","Added permanent rich rule in public zone rejecting tcp/9000 from all other sources","Reloaded firewalld and verified both permanent and runtime configs match","Started a Python2 SimpleHTTPServer on node1:9000 and verified node2 gets HTTP 200 while node3 gets connection refused; verified SSH banner reachable from node3","Captured pre-restart boot_id and firewalld health baseline on all three nodes","Restarted node1 via deferred systemd-run systemctl reboot, polled until SSH returned, confirmed new boot_id and firewalld config/behavior intact","Restarted node2 via same mechanism, confirmed new boot_id","Restarted node3 via same mechanism, confirmed new boot_id","Re-ran end-to-end connectivity verification (node2 allowed on 9000, node3 rejected on 9000, node3 SSH allowed) after all three nodes were back online","Cleaned up the temporary test HTTP listener on node1"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Persistent firewalld enabled on node1 with SSH allowed from any address","command_ids":["cmd-79139068cbdd43f6","cmd-ec203a2e7ce549d6"],"summary":"firewalld active+enabled; public zone list-all shows ssh service allowed with no source restriction"},{"requirement":"TCP 9000 allowed only from node2 (10.100.140.11), permanent config","command_ids":["cmd-aa800845d19b441b","cmd